      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "IDOR in Event Category Updates\n\nThe endpoint for updating an event (`PUT /api/admin/events/[id]`) does not verify that the categories being updated actually belong to the event. An attacker with edit access to any event can modify category details (name, distance, price, limits) across the entire platform by supplying target category IDs in their payload."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/app/api/admin/events/[id]/route.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 204,
                  "endLine": 206
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Use `updateMany` to securely restrict category updates to the current event"
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/api/admin/events/[id]",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/app/api/admin/events/[id]/route.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 204,
                        "endLine": 206
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "if (cat.id) {\n          await prisma.category.updateMany({\n            where: { id: cat.id, eventId: id },"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "Update the category loop in the `PUT` handler to use `prisma.category.updateMany` with `eventId: id` in the `where` clause. This ensures that the category being updated actually belongs to the event being edited.",
                "markdown": "Update the category loop in the `PUT` handler to use `prisma.category.updateMany` with `eventId: id` in the `where` clause. This ensures that the category being updated actually belongs to the event being edited."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "333b15ce03c20ca33e59a3d6df086bc41f5f8638e420b0b3784ddb03b888f218"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "7.1",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "3174e38e6c72ef9ffcecc7abfdfb44ac425908b43bf07eeb479e0aacf5dcaf79",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0001",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 7.1,
              "timestamp": "2026-09-23 01:54:16 UTC",
              "target": "/workspace/run-as-one",
              "endpoint": "/api/admin/events/[id]",
              "method": "PUT",
              "cwe": "CWE-862",
              "impact": "An attacker with `event:edit` access on a single event can modify the details (name, distance, price, slot limits, inclusions) of any category belonging to any other event or organization. This allows sabotage of competing events by changing their pricing, removing slot limits, or altering category inclusions.",
              "technical_analysis": "In `src/app/api/admin/events/[id]/route.ts` (PUT handler), the application updates existing event categories using a loop over the provided `categories` array. For each category with an `id`, it executes a `prisma.category.update({ where: { id: cat.id }, data: { ... } })` call. Because the `where` clause only specifies `id` and does not enforce `eventId: id`, the query blindly updates any category in the database matching the provided ID, bypassing the event and organizer authorization checks performed earlier in the request.",
              "remediation_steps": "Update the category loop in the `PUT` handler to use `prisma.category.updateMany` with `eventId: id` in the `where` clause. This ensures that the category being updated actually belongs to the event being edited.",
              "counterevidence": "The endpoint correctly restricts category deletions to the current event by using `eventId: id`. However, the subsequent loop that processes category updates directly calls `prisma.category.update` using only the provided `cat.id`. The lack of an `eventId: id` check in this update operation constitutes a concrete, bypassable authorization boundary.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "If category IDs are treated as highly unpredictable secrets not exposed anywhere, the likelihood of exploitation is reduced. However, category IDs are typically public in registration flows.",
              "fix_verification": "I have verified that changing `update` to `updateMany` with `where: { id: cat.id, eventId: id }` securely limits the update to categories belonging to the event currently being edited. A malicious payload containing an external category ID will not match any rows in `updateMany` and will thus perform no operation, safely ignoring the IDOR attempt while preserving legitimate updates.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Log in as an Organizer or Event Manager with `event:edit` permissions for at least one event.\n2. Identify the `id` of a category belonging to another organization's event (e.g., from the public registration page).\n3. Send a `PUT` request to `/api/admin/events/<your_event_id>` to edit your own event.\n4. In the JSON payload, include a `categories` array containing an object with the victim category's `id` along with modified values (e.g., `price: 1`).\n5. The server updates the victim's category with the new values.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-287",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "PayMongo Webhook Signature Authentication Bypass via Missing Header\n\nThe PayMongo webhook endpoint (`/api/webhooks/paymongo`) skips signature verification if the `paymongo-signature` header is omitted, allowing attackers to forge successful payment events and mark arbitrary registrations as PAID."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/app/api/webhooks/paymongo/route.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 14,
                  "endLine": 36
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/app/api/webhooks/paymongo/route.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 14,
                        "endLine": 36
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "if (webhookSecret) {\n      if (!signatureHeader) {\n        return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Missing signature header' }, { status: 400 });\n      }\n\n      // Verify signature\n      // Signature header format: t=1611234567,te=signature_hash,li=test_signature_hash\n      const timestampMatch = signatureHeader.match(/t=([^,]+)/);\n      const signatureMatch = signatureHeader.match(/te=([^,]+)/) || signatureHeader.match(/li=([^,]+)/);\n\n      if (!timestampMatch || !signatureMatch) {\n        return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Invalid signature format' }, { status: 400 });\n      }\n\n      const timestamp = timestampMatch[1];\n      const signature = signatureMatch[1];\n\n      const signaturePayload = `${timestamp}.${rawBody}`;\n      const computedSignature = crypto\n        .createHmac('sha256', webhookSecret)\n        .update(signaturePayload)\n        .digest('hex');\n\n      if (computedSignature !== signature) {\n        console.error('PayMongo Webhook signature verification failed');\n        return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Invalid signature' }, { status: 400 });\n      }\n    }"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "Ensure that if the `PAYMONGO_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is configured, the `paymongo-signature` header is strictly required. If the header is missing, the request should be rejected immediately.",
                "markdown": "Ensure that if the `PAYMONGO_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is configured, the `paymongo-signature` header is strictly required. If the header is missing, the request should be rejected immediately."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "e9d91b6c213f0e81393ce68f18daf65477821a1298dc9d5d83f02f32a969edca"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "7.5",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "8fe129a77fcf3e1a93135feaec2c3b542075677e620a3b17bfd4ccb55106a85a",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0002",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 7.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-09-23 01:54:37 UTC",
              "target": "/workspace/run-as-one",
              "cwe": "CWE-287",
              "impact": "An attacker can completely bypass payment for any registration by forging a webhook payload pointing to their `orderRef` or `checkoutSessionId`, granting them free access to events and resulting in direct financial loss for the organizers.",
              "technical_analysis": "The vulnerability stems from flawed conditional logic during signature verification. The code intends to skip verification only if `PAYMONGO_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is not set (e.g., in a local development environment). However, the condition `if (webhookSecret && signatureHeader)` also skips verification if the `signatureHeader` is missing from the incoming request. Since an attacker controls the HTTP headers, they can simply omit `paymongo-signature`, bypass the HMAC validation entirely, and inject arbitrary JSON payloads representing successful payments.",
              "remediation_steps": "Ensure that if the `PAYMONGO_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is configured, the `paymongo-signature` header is strictly required. If the header is missing, the request should be rejected immediately.",
              "counterevidence": "I checked if there is any middleware or other validation that enforces the presence of the `paymongo-signature` header. There is none. If the header is omitted, the `signatureHeader` variable is null, the `if (webhookSecret && signatureHeader)` block is completely bypassed, and the execution flows directly to processing the JSON payload and updating the database to `PAID`.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "If the application uses a different payment gateway in production that does not rely on this webhook, the impact would be reduced. However, this is the primary payment mechanism implemented.",
              "fix_verification": "I reviewed the code logic and confirmed that replacing the conditional block prevents the bypass. If the webhook secret is configured, the updated code strictly demands the signature header and its valid format, rejecting requests immediately with a 400 Bad Request if they are missing or malformed. Legitimate webhooks sent by PayMongo contain the header and will pass the verification.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Create a pending registration and obtain its `orderRef` (e.g., `RM-1234567`).\n2. Send a POST request to `/api/webhooks/paymongo` with the payload simulating a successful payment for that `orderRef`.\n3. Do not include the `paymongo-signature` header in the request.\n4. The server responds with `{\"received\": true}` and marks the registration as `PAID`.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
