          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/app/api/auth/logout/route.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 1,
                        "endLine": 7
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';\nimport prisma from '@/lib/db';\nimport { clearAuthCookie } from '@/lib/auth';\nimport { getActor, sessionsCutoff } from '@/lib/actor';\nimport { recordAudit } from '@/lib/audit';\n\nexport async function POST() {\n  const actor = await getActor();\n  \n  if (actor) {\n    const sessionsValidFrom = sessionsCutoff();\n    const isStaff = actor.kind === 'STAFF';\n\n    await prisma.$transaction(async tx => {\n      if (isStaff) {\n        await tx.staffAccount.update({ where: { id: actor.id }, data: { sessionsValidFrom } });\n      } else {\n        await tx.organizer.update({ where: { id: actor.id }, data: { sessionsValidFrom } });\n      }\n      await recordAudit(tx, actor, {\n        action: 'auth.logged_out',\n        entityType: isStaff ? 'StaffAccount' : 'Organizer',\n        entityId: actor.id,\n        summary: 'Signed out.',\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  await clearAuthCookie();\n  return NextResponse.json({ success: true }, { status: 200 });\n}"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "Update the logout route to invalidate the session on the server side. Since the application uses a stateless JWT without individual session IDs, the most straightforward fix using the existing schema is to update the user's `sessionsValidFrom` timestamp to the current time, identical to the \"Sign out other devices\" functionality. This ensures the JWT is rejected by `getActor()` on subsequent requests.",
                "markdown": "Update the logout route to invalidate the session on the server side. Since the application uses a stateless JWT without individual session IDs, the most straightforward fix using the existing schema is to update the user's `sessionsValidFrom` timestamp to the current time, identical to the \"Sign out other devices\" functionality. This ensures the JWT is rejected by `getActor()` on subsequent requests."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "30438cbc93579306c9bc9da1060a665e6bc1efc409d30241f345c6b0a2ac13dd"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "4.2",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "58f9abad95e708fcac631cc506a5114328fc6e4b46f066cd8e7931bf7090f044",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0006",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 4.2,
              "timestamp": "2026-09-23 01:55:58 UTC",
              "target": "Logout Endpoint (src/app/api/auth/logout/route.ts)",
              "cwe": "CWE-613",
              "impact": "If a user's JWT is stolen (e.g. via XSS, network interception, or local access), the attacker can continue to access the account until the token expires, even if the legitimate user attempts to terminate the session by logging out.",
              "technical_analysis": "The application uses stateless JWTs for session management, stored in an `httpOnly` cookie. The logout endpoint (`/api/auth/logout/route.ts`) simply calls `clearAuthCookie()`, which instructs the browser to delete the cookie. However, the JWT itself remains valid according to its cryptographic signature and expiration time (1 day).\n\nBecause the server does not track individual JWTs, it cannot natively invalidate a specific token. However, the application already implements a mechanism to invalidate all of a user's active tokens by updating the `sessionsValidFrom` timestamp in the database (used in `/api/admin/profile/sessions/route.ts`). Failing to update this timestamp during a normal logout means the token remains usable by anyone who manages to acquire it.",
              "remediation_steps": "Update the logout route to invalidate the session on the server side. Since the application uses a stateless JWT without individual session IDs, the most straightforward fix using the existing schema is to update the user's `sessionsValidFrom` timestamp to the current time, identical to the \"Sign out other devices\" functionality. This ensures the JWT is rejected by `getActor()` on subsequent requests.",
              "counterevidence": "The JWT has a natural expiration time of 1 day, which limits the window of opportunity for an attacker. Furthermore, the application provides a \"Sign out other devices\" feature which does correctly update `sessionsValidFrom`.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "If the JWT expiration time was significantly longer (e.g., weeks or months), the impact would be much higher, raising the severity.",
              "fix_verification": "1. Applicability: The patch updates the logout route to use the existing `sessionsValidFrom` mechanism.\n2. Security closure: A stolen JWT will be rejected by `getActor()` (via the `issuedBefore(session.iat, sessionsValidFrom)` check) after the user has logged out.\n3. Bypass review: No alternative logout mechanisms exist that bypass this.\n4. Preserved behavior: The user is still successfully logged out and the cookie is cleared.\n5. Repository checks: The Prisma schema and actor functions are used identically to existing code.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Log into the application and extract the JWT from the `admin_token` cookie.\n2. Log out of the application using the `/api/auth/logout` endpoint.\n3. Attempt to access a protected route (e.g., `/api/admin/profile`) by manually providing the extracted JWT in the `admin_token` cookie.\n4. The server accepts the token and processes the request successfully, proving the token was not invalidated.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
